    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "92480e0c_8067a75a",
        "filename": "include/gpio.h",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 38,
      "author": {
        "id": 1136059
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-06-13T17:33:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I figured that the common flag combinations is basically the same as using that. It makes it easier for us to parse the flags, because cr50 uses splits it into a high/low bit and a edge bit.",
      "parentUuid": "12869fd4_0f5d870a",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 38,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 38,
        "endChar": 36
      },
      "revId": "bf9c3217ee3e865f720f63d070dcdb799251cd59",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c6f2bba5_630d45b2",
        "filename": "include/gpio.h",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 38,
      "author": {
        "id": 1283719
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-01-23T02:27:40Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m removing this, and bring line 55 and 56 to here.\nWith that, we can have 1:1 mapping between GPIO_HIB_WAKE_\u003ccond\u003e and DIO_WAKE_\u003ccond\u003e.\nParsing can be plainer and readable, imho.",
      "parentUuid": "92480e0c_8067a75a",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 38,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 38,
        "endChar": 36
      },
      "revId": "bf9c3217ee3e865f720f63d070dcdb799251cd59",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "13255f97_69b9c8fb",
        "filename": "include/gpio.h",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 39,
      "author": {
        "id": 1125984
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-06-13T19:50:44Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Having a disable flag seems weird to me. Why can\u0027t the board just enable/disable when it wants to?",
      "revId": "bf9c3217ee3e865f720f63d070dcdb799251cd59",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "5b8cd7c4_9288cd70",
        "filename": "include/gpio.h",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 39,
      "author": {
        "id": 1136059
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-06-13T21:47:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "What do you mean?\n\nI added the explicit disable flag, because these are new flags and I don\u0027t want to make someone omitting GPIO_HIB_WAKE flags to disable the wake pins silently. So If you run gpio_set_flag(GPIO_PULL_UP) or something then you dont also need to be aware that that signal is attached to a wake pin and what type it is.",
      "parentUuid": "13255f97_69b9c8fb",
      "revId": "bf9c3217ee3e865f720f63d070dcdb799251cd59",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e074a95a_1feb53a4",
        "filename": "include/gpio.h",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 39,
      "author": {
        "id": 1125984
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-06-14T00:47:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It\u0027s weird in the sense that usually boards define a list of GPIOs that are their wake pins, and then during init, configure those pins to be so. Having a flag that means \"don\u0027t enable a GPIO as wake pin\" seemed weird, as my first reaction would be to not set it up as a wake pin in the first place.\n\nI guess this is slightly different in that the cr50 board may want to change the wake pins at any time...\n\nWhat do you think about keeping the hibernate enable/disable separate from modifying the GPIO flags? That way, setting a pull up for example, won\u0027t affect the hibernate config.\n\nOr is there something that I\u0027m missing?",
      "parentUuid": "5b8cd7c4_9288cd70",
      "revId": "bf9c3217ee3e865f720f63d070dcdb799251cd59",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a5181ac6_80e64235",
        "filename": "include/gpio.h",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 39,
      "author": {
        "id": 1136059
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-06-16T16:40:38Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It is not a flag that says don\u0027t enable the wake pin. It is used to disable the wake pin if it is set.",
      "parentUuid": "e074a95a_1feb53a4",
      "revId": "bf9c3217ee3e865f720f63d070dcdb799251cd59",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9d71ba2e_f775d1e9",
        "filename": "include/gpio.h",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 39,
      "author": {
        "id": 1125984
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-06-19T17:01:13Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Oh, okay. I feel like keeping the wake en/disable separate from the other GPIO settings wouldn\u0027t require the flag, but I can understand this implementation.",
      "parentUuid": "a5181ac6_80e64235",
      "revId": "bf9c3217ee3e865f720f63d070dcdb799251cd59",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
